{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_audits_2026_09_25_project_audit", "label": "Conductor Project Audit (2026-09-25)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/audits/2026-09-25-project-audit.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": "2026-09-25", "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}, {"id": "docs_audits_2026_09_25_project_audit_a1_verification_conflict", "label": "A1: Conflicting verification-scope rules", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/audits/2026-09-25-project-audit.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Contradiction between a mandatory full test/lint run at task completion and the allowance to skip verification of an untouched module, plus general integrity checks assigned to every task; proposed fix is that verification scope should track changed behavior, consumers, config and risk, not the act of committing, pushing or re-confirming."}, {"id": "docs_audits_2026_09_25_project_audit_a2_adapter_exception_loss", "label": "A2: Shortened adapter rules drop Claude-specific exceptions", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/audits/2026-09-25-project-audit.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The Claude playbook exempts re-disabling a fix for a test on small tasks, but the shared adapters/core-body.md text used to generate other environments' rules requires the procedure unconditionally for any fix, so patching only the Claude playbook does not fix other environments."}, {"id": "docs_audits_2026_09_25_project_audit_a3_head_rollback_defect", "label": "A3: HEAD rollback does not restore original task state", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/audits/2026-09-25-project-audit.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "debugging.md proposes HEAD as both the original version and a manual restore target, but an untracked file has no HEAD version, and with an already-dirty working tree HEAD is not equal to the pre-task state either; statically confirmed procedural defect, not an observed data-loss incident."}, {"id": "docs_audits_2026_09_25_project_audit_a4_context_truncation", "label": "A4: Lessons-inject truncation hides newest lessons and index link", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/audits/2026-09-25-project-audit.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The hook selects the last eight inbox lines then appends the index link; when the block exceeds the budget it keeps the beginning and truncates the end, so the newest selected lessons and the index reference disappear first. Reproduced synthetically: HOOK_CONTROL index=true; LONG index=false newest=false older=true; chars=2986."}, {"id": "docs_audits_2026_09_25_project_audit_a5_memory_maintenance_gap", "label": "A5: Memory maintenance playbook needs an absent dev tree", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/audits/2026-09-25-project-audit.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The installed distill playbook calls a migration tool, repo checks, reinstall and commit, but those tools live only in the source repository, not the installed runtime (tools/, qa/, install.sh absent from the installed folder); migration tested with preserved_valid=2 preserved_invalid=1 retained_prior=1, first_index_entry=undated, revealing undated entries sort above dated ones though the index claims newest-first order."}, {"id": "docs_audits_2026_09_25_project_audit_a6_backup_restore_incomplete", "label": "A6: Local backup restore instructions are incomplete", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/audits/2026-09-25-project-audit.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Restore instructions copy lessons and some data but do not restore backup-push.sh or .gitignore, and do not recreate the scheduler task; the final `git reset --soft` only moves HEAD and does not bring back missing files, so a successful last push does not prove restorability on a clean machine."}, {"id": "docs_audits_2026_09_25_project_audit_a7_graph_stale", "label": "A7: Graphify graph is structurally valid but content-stale", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/audits/2026-09-25-project-audit.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "362 nodes, 647 edges, unique ids, no dangling edge endpoints, all source paths exist; but 12 of 85 manifest files (installer, CI, README, three playbooks) have hashes mismatching current bytes, and install-companions.sh is missing from the manifest entirely: 73 matches, 12 mismatches, 0 missing files checked."}, {"id": "docs_audits_2026_09_25_project_audit_a8_uninstall_no_stop_on_copy_failure", "label": "A8: Failed lesson copy does not stop uninstall", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/audits/2026-09-25-project-audit.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The uninstall action wrapper prints a copy error but does not abort subsequent directory deletion; a sandboxed run with copy replaced to always fail still selected the whole Conductor directory for removal and reported success with exit code 0 (no real files were deleted in the test). On the real machine, backup script, project memory snapshots and local git history also live in the deleted folder and --keep-lessons does not preserve them."}, {"id": "docs_audits_2026_09_25_project_audit_installer_defects_table", "label": "Other confirmed installer/uninstaller defects", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/audits/2026-09-25-project-audit.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}, {"id": "docs_audits_2026_09_25_project_audit_qa_diagnostics_unreliable", "label": "QA/diagnostic tooling accepts unproven success", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/audits/2026-09-25-project-audit.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "None of the journal, benchmark runner, doctor script or lint distinguish an observed command from proven test execution: a printed `npm test` line is logged PASS partial without running; a masked non-zero shell exit after error handling is logged PASS partial; a failed benchmark experiment (fake Claude exit 7, empty JSON, zero repeats) still ends with exit 0 and 'done'; an empty playbooks folder passes doctor's check; lint depends on path spacing and checks thresholds without checking that declarations still exist."}, {"id": "docs_audits_2026_09_25_project_audit_sed_portability_issue", "label": "install.sh sed -i form may be non-portable to macOS/BSD sed", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/audits/2026-09-25-project-audit.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "install.sh uses the GNU form of `sed -i` without an extension argument; Apple's sed manual requires that argument. Not reproduced on macOS in this audit, so platform support is unconfirmed rather than disproven."}, {"id": "external_cursor_hooks_docs", "label": "Cursor hooks official documentation", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/audits/2026-09-25-project-audit.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": "https://prod.cursor.com/docs/hooks", "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}, {"id": "external_apple_sed_docs", "label": "Apple sed manual (text_cmds)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/audits/2026-09-25-project-audit.md", "sour